    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27629" root="ظلف" body-key="Z">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ظَلَفَةٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ظَلْفٌ</span>, in two places, near the beginning. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Hence, perhaps,] one says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَقَامَهُ ٱللّٰهُ</span>,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلَى الظَّلَفَاتِ</span>, (TA, [there said to be <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُحَرَّكَة</span>,])
or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الظلِفات</span>, (so in a copy of the T, [i. e.
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الظَّلِفَاتِ</span></b> ,]) meaning [<i>God made him to keep to</i>]
<i>a state of hardship and straitness.</i> (T, TA.)

